WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:01.500
- Let's get to something sure to bring

00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:03.710
a little more joy to
your day, well hopefully.

00:00:03.710 --> 00:00:04.788
This is What I'm Liking.

00:00:04.788 --> 00:00:07.730
(jazzy musical intro)

00:00:07.730 --> 00:00:09.840
That starts with a
videographer named Tonda.

00:00:09.840 --> 00:00:12.260
She walked into a room to
find her three-year-old son

00:00:12.260 --> 00:00:13.650
jumping on their coffee table.

00:00:13.650 --> 00:00:16.200
He was mimicking a cartoon on the TV.

00:00:16.200 --> 00:00:18.360
Not surprisingly, the table broke.

00:00:18.360 --> 00:00:20.850
That turned out to be a
pivotal moment for Tonda.

00:00:20.850 --> 00:00:22.240
Instead of buying a new table,

00:00:22.240 --> 00:00:25.000
she set out to make a new one herself.

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:26.870
I should point out that
she'd never actually

00:00:26.870 --> 00:00:28.490
built anything before,

00:00:28.490 --> 00:00:31.150
but that first table led
to a full fledged business

00:00:31.150 --> 00:00:33.220
and a way to give back to the community.

00:00:33.220 --> 00:00:35.560
From She Slangs Wood,
let's say hi to Tonda

00:00:35.560 --> 00:00:37.420
who watches it 3:00 PM on our partner

00:00:37.420 --> 00:00:39.658
station TMJ4, what's up?

00:00:39.658 --> 00:00:41.908
(cheering)

00:00:43.070 --> 00:00:44.470
- What's up, Kelly? How you doin?

00:00:44.470 --> 00:00:46.490
- I am so good, but oh my gosh,

00:00:46.490 --> 00:00:49.290
I have to lead with, you are
such a beautiful lot of a woman

00:00:49.290 --> 00:00:50.380
and I like your shop.

00:00:50.380 --> 00:00:52.730
That looks fun and I
want to build something.

00:00:52.730 --> 00:00:56.410
So how did this grow from one
table into a whole business?

00:00:56.410 --> 00:00:58.860
- You know, I am so proud that

00:00:58.860 --> 00:01:00.460
just from watching YouTube videos,

00:01:00.460 --> 00:01:02.183
I was able to build a table, right?

00:01:02.183 --> 00:01:03.117
(laughter)

00:01:03.117 --> 00:01:05.350
I made a Facebook post and

00:01:06.430 --> 00:01:09.460
unexpectedly, about 30 requests later,

00:01:09.460 --> 00:01:10.530
there were 30 people asking me

00:01:10.530 --> 00:01:11.640
to build the same table for them.

00:01:11.640 --> 00:01:13.710
You know, it was quite wild, quite wild.

00:01:13.710 --> 00:01:15.970
And we were in the middle of the pandemic,

00:01:15.970 --> 00:01:18.533
I wasn't making the same amount
of money as I normally make

00:01:18.533 --> 00:01:20.070
with my business.

00:01:20.070 --> 00:01:21.960
I decided, hey, I can make,

00:01:21.960 --> 00:01:24.840
I can sell 300, $400 each with the table

00:01:24.840 --> 00:01:25.720
and pay my bills.

00:01:25.720 --> 00:01:28.090
And, you know, it was a
survival tactic, you know?

00:01:28.090 --> 00:01:29.180
- Oh my gosh, by the way,

00:01:29.180 --> 00:01:30.770
I loved all those tables that I just saw.

00:01:30.770 --> 00:01:31.940
That's why they're asking.

00:01:31.940 --> 00:01:33.490
I love the wide plank on the top,

00:01:33.490 --> 00:01:35.360
that was, I might want one.

00:01:35.360 --> 00:01:38.280
So you're teaching your
community these skills as well,

00:01:38.280 --> 00:01:39.320
right?

00:01:39.320 --> 00:01:40.153
- Absolutely.

00:01:40.153 --> 00:01:42.070
So, She Slangs Wood,

00:01:42.070 --> 00:01:45.870
since the pandemic has kind
of eased up a little bit,

00:01:45.870 --> 00:01:49.030
I have turned it into more
of a mentorship program.

00:01:49.030 --> 00:01:50.050
I want to teach women like,

00:01:50.050 --> 00:01:51.560
hey, you can do this yourself.

00:01:51.560 --> 00:01:54.010
You don't have to wait for
anybody to do this type of work,

00:01:54.010 --> 00:01:56.220
you can do it yourself.

00:01:56.220 --> 00:01:58.440
With the money that we
raised with She Slangs Wood,

00:01:58.440 --> 00:02:00.150
I was able to purchase a building

00:02:00.150 --> 00:02:02.550
within the Harambee
neighborhood, here in Milwaukee,

00:02:02.550 --> 00:02:04.660
which is near and dear to our community.

00:02:04.660 --> 00:02:07.290
I'm able to do that type of
work with the community members

00:02:07.290 --> 00:02:08.450
in our neighborhood.

00:02:08.450 --> 00:02:10.580
The overall goal is to eliminate poverty

00:02:10.580 --> 00:02:11.600
within that neighborhood.

00:02:11.600 --> 00:02:13.390
And we want to create some dollars

00:02:13.390 --> 00:02:16.120
and we want people to be just
uplifted in that neighborhood,

00:02:16.120 --> 00:02:16.953
pretty much.

00:02:16.953 --> 00:02:18.820
- That's a beautiful thing
and a beautiful idea.

00:02:18.820 --> 00:02:21.381
I want you to have a TV
show and I would watch it.

00:02:21.381 --> 00:02:22.214
(laughter)

00:02:22.214 --> 00:02:23.600
Thank you so much Tonda.

00:02:23.600 --> 00:02:26.883
I'm liking your post right now, right?

00:02:26.883 --> 00:02:28.350
- Thank you.

00:02:28.350 --> 00:02:29.580
- All right, well, that's not all

00:02:29.580 --> 00:02:31.300
our season long partner Pilot Pen,

00:02:31.300 --> 00:02:32.950
the go-to pen of the Kelly Clarkson show,

00:02:32.950 --> 00:02:35.350
likes to celebrate those
who create fearlessly,

00:02:35.350 --> 00:02:36.800
just like you ma'am.

00:02:36.800 --> 00:02:38.750
So they'll be using their
friction erasable pen

00:02:38.750 --> 00:02:40.530
to write you a check for $1,000,

00:02:40.530 --> 00:02:41.862
how's that sound?

00:02:41.862 --> 00:02:44.039
(cheering)

00:02:44.039 --> 00:02:44.872
- Yes!

